Get the default partitioning schema for the given offer ID and OS ID.

USAGE:
  scw baremetal partitioning-schemas get-default [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  [offer-id]        ID of the offer
  [os-id]           ID of the OS
  [zone=fr-par-1]   Zone to target. If none is passed will use default zone from the config (fr-par-1 | fr-par-2 | nl-ams-1 | nl-ams-2 | pl-waw-2 | pl-waw-3)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for get-default
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use
